{"data": [{"author_id": "849987588073062401", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:01:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118478745883582895"], "id": "2118478745883582895", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus https://t.co/BHeuMq2CHC", "url": "https://x.com/BlackthorneAI/status/2118478745883582895"}, {"author_id": "1106896608", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:56:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118477572904468560"], "id": "2118477572904468560", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 26, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus AI can drastically speed up science. \n\nThe one on the left is an anabolic androgenic steroid designed to be less androgenic so females can also take this. \n\nThis is medicine. (Unproven, untested, I make zero claims and invite any labs or biotechs who wish this to have it. Someone https://t.co/tK0EfBRtnx", "url": "https://x.com/Chaos2Cured/status/2118477572904468560"}, {"author_id": "225100450", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:44:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118474486538489872"], "id": "2118474486538489872", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 31, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus The AI finished the research. The humans are still deleting the interesting parts.", "url": "https://x.com/ExiledonMoon/status/2118474486538489872"}, {"author_id": "2091334614786752512", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:39:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118473182181298585"], "id": "2118473182181298585", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Curious whether the report splits the speedup by task type. Writing code and running evals are easy to speed up and easy to measure. Picking the next experiment is the part that would change the pace if AI starts doing it well.", "url": "https://x.com/contentmation/status/2118473182181298585"}, {"author_id": "737020788566433792", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:37:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118472854027300990"], "id": "2118472854027300990", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus 1.9x faster R&amp;D because the models are helping write the next ones. The feedback loop is no longer a slide.", "url": "https://x.com/terpcoinn/status/2118472854027300990"}, {"author_id": "29677918", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:32:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118471586822901998"], "id": "2118471586822901998", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus When Anthropic uses its own models to speed research, the flywheel is real.", "url": "https://x.com/hotmob/status/2118471586822901998"}, {"author_id": "1701689703626412032", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:29:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118470866006643072"], "id": "2118470866006643072", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 29, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Research speeding up is the real story", "url": "https://x.com/MichaelKaiserAI/status/2118470866006643072"}, {"author_id": "1838558231590830080", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:26:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118469979352002638"], "id": "2118469979352002638", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus If Anthropic publishes its own AI-speedup analysis next to METR, what number would actually surprise you at this point?", "url": "https://x.com/Righteousbeing7/status/2118469979352002638"}, {"author_id": "2115497882585645056", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:17:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118467699344883931"], "id": "2118467699344883931", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus 'Independent' gets a lot less independent when the most informative evidence is redacted.", "url": "https://x.com/kiteze2x/status/2118467699344883931"}, {"author_id": "1690404505492353024", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:12:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118466388884939199"], "id": "2118466388884939199", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 51, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus https://t.co/b9XN04gOW3", "url": "https://x.com/henriquetxz/status/2118466388884939199"}, {"author_id": "1721496460053635072", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:11:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118466206344880408"], "id": "2118466206344880408", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus AI is speeding Anthropic's research.\nThey'll publish how much. Not how.", "url": "https://x.com/buildsinews/status/2118466206344880408"}, {"author_id": "2116355353327587329", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:11:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118466139626062124"], "id": "2118466139626062124", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus The part of that report worth reading will be where AI didn't speed things up. The labs are the best-case users, so whatever stayed slow there will stay slow everywhere.", "url": "https://x.com/XWolfHQ/status/2118466139626062124"}, {"author_id": "1855995202001092608", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:11:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118466135020523904"], "id": "2118466135020523904", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 26, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Let’s say data center permitting for 2029+ flat lines for a few years, what impact do you think that has on this pace of progress? How much progress runway do we have left on existing permitted capacity through 2027/2028?\n\nDo you think expectations of less data centers and", "url": "https://x.com/Big_Picture_89/status/2118466135020523904"}, {"author_id": "1708492008673722368", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:10:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118466092200800619"], "id": "2118466092200800619", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 44, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Curious to see how much detail they actually share.", "url": "https://x.com/annanidev/status/2118466092200800619"}, {"author_id": "302555661", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:10:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118466010709905851"], "id": "2118466010709905851", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Fascinating that internal views match METR's. @TALERTSX04 has been tracking this acceleration closely.", "url": "https://x.com/yuricandid0/status/2118466010709905851"}, {"author_id": "2116579414813065216", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:09:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118465827053932605"], "id": "2118465827053932605", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus mccandlish basically said the redactions are the point. sharing what drives the speedup hands everyone else a roadmap. their own report is the one that matters now.", "url": "https://x.com/ContextWindowed/status/2118465827053932605"}, {"author_id": "417508671", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:09:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118465698481779057"], "id": "2118465698481779057", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Letting METR look inside the research process is the part I’m cheering for here.", "url": "https://x.com/thesimaximalist/status/2118465698481779057"}, {"author_id": "1596337163805020160", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:08:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118465415177498665"], "id": "2118465415177498665", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 103, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus AI helping researchers build better AI creates some fascinating questions", "url": "https://x.com/nrqa__/status/2118465415177498665"}, {"author_id": "2103389296145448960", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:05:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118464709531934977"], "id": "2118464709531934977", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Founder confirmation plus METR beats either signal alone. The open question is whether that 2x shows up in shipping cadence or only in internal eval deltas. When do outsiders get a yardstick that isn't another lab slide?", "url": "https://x.com/Aistarjohn/status/2118464709531934977"}, {"author_id": "95484415", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:04:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118464454622941261"], "id": "2118464454622941261", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus The useful bit is the report, not the claim. Numbers beat vibes.", "url": "https://x.com/cdepino/status/2118464454622941261"}, {"author_id": "2081555588547502080", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:02:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118464059066523960"], "id": "2118464059066523960", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus McCandlish confirming METR's read from inside is the datapoint that matters — an external 1.9x acceleration estimate lining up with the internal view is harder to dismiss than either alone. The test is Anthropic's own analysis, due in the coming weeks: will it publish a", "url": "https://x.com/TMZXIH/status/2118464059066523960"}, {"author_id": "1679837305409007617", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:02:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118463940678017485"], "id": "2118463940678017485", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Per Reuters, METR's 11-week review found @AnthropicAI benchmark progress about 1.9x faster since Oct 2025, and said AI is not yet making highly significant fully autonomous training contributions.", "url": "https://x.com/BroadwakeAI/status/2118463940678017485"}, {"author_id": "1165159200470650881", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:02:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118463940107911630"], "id": "2118463940107911630", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 24, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus What I'd want in that report is the redacted stuff. METR says Anthropic \"redacted a majority of the evidence we found most informative.\" If Anthropic's own analysis shows some of that, it's the real news.", "url": "https://x.com/AIQuanting/status/2118463940107911630"}, {"author_id": "1553835048", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:01:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118463809090359744"], "id": "2118463809090359744", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus will read it", "url": "https://x.com/leononrails/status/2118463809090359744"}, {"author_id": "2088718703026221056", "conversation_id": "2118460897966338116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:00:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118463586628518065"], "id": "2118463586628518065", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 82, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus really wanna see their own numbers compared to METR’s findings", "url": "https://x.com/realivann/status/2118463586628518065"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "849987588073062401", "name": "₿lackthorne AI", "username": "BlackthorneAI"}, {"id": "1106896608", "name": "Kirk Patrick Miller", "username": "Chaos2Cured"}, {"id": "225100450", "name": "The Lunar Misfit", "username": "ExiledonMoon"}, {"id